# Source propagation tools for the nonbinary symplectic branch

The selected backward paths use the actual source conjugators and local
stabilizer quotient. The small normal-section action is proved without
splitting a central extension. The central propagation retains its full
fixed intersection, as required by the nonbinary argument.

These are proved parts of MS93 (5.7) and the propagation used in (5.10).
They do not assert (5.8)--(5.11) or a bound on the critical distance.
The remaining radius-displacement and chosen-generator inputs are explicit
in the consumers and must be discharged by the source assembly.
